## Project 04 — Fixed Random Forest Comparison on EGFR

A restrained Random Forest baseline was evaluated on the exact frozen Day 03 ChEMBL EGFR dataset, Morgan fingerprints, labels, and random/scaffold test assignments.

### Fixed comparison design

- Same **7,757** curated EGFR structures.
- Same radius-2, 2,048-bit Morgan fingerprints.
- Same frozen random and Bemis–Murcko scaffold splits.
- No test-set hyperparameter tuning.
- Random Forest configuration: 500 trees, `sqrt` features, minimum leaf size 2, class weighting, seed 42.

### Key result

| Split | Model | ROC-AUC | PR-AUC | MCC | F1 | Brier score |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Random | Logistic Regression | 0.9097 | 0.9715 | 0.6314 | 0.9195 | 0.0976 |
| Random | Random Forest | 0.9398 | 0.9830 | 0.6731 | 0.9343 | 0.0787 |
| Scaffold | Logistic Regression | 0.8906 | 0.9643 | 0.5949 | 0.9084 | 0.1096 |
| Scaffold | Random Forest | 0.9410 | 0.9837 | 0.6618 | 0.9303 | 0.0816 |

Random Forest made **33 fewer errors** on the random test split and **45 fewer errors** on the scaffold test split at the fixed 0.50 threshold. It is the leading internal predictive baseline in this fixed comparison.

This remains an internal public-data evaluation—not external, prospective, clinical, safety, efficacy, or drug-discovery validation.

